Milestone 9 — Tasks 9.5–9.8

This bundle adds service-layer tracing, Reddit external-operation tracing, PostgreSQL spans, and the Loki logging architecture documentation.

Prerequisite

The repository should already include the Milestone 9 tasks 9.1–9.4 OpenTelemetry foundation and HTTP tracing middleware. The current source changes use the global OpenTelemetry API established by that foundation.

Trace hierarchy

The intended worker-driven ingestion trace is:

HTTP server span
-> reddit.ingest
-> reddit.authenticate
-> reddit.ingest_listing
-> reddit.fetch_listing
-> reddit.normalize
-> reddit.deduplicate
-> external_item.upsert_batch
-> db.query

Service requests follow:

HTTP server span
-> community.create|get|list|update|delete
-> db.query
## Important baseline note

The latest repository archive supplied for this task did not contain the previously discussed `internal/telemetry` package or OpenTelemetry module dependencies. To keep this bundle internally consistent, the bundle includes the 9.1–9.4 foundation files as prerequisites, plus the 9.5–9.8 changes.

If those 9.1–9.4 files are already present in the working tree, treat the corresponding files in this bundle as the matching source-of-truth version rather than merging duplicate implementations.

